[THOUGHT] Smoking has been ruled out, narrowing environmental/occupational contributors. The next critical gap is objective clinical evidence: physical examination findings are essential to support bronchiectasis (e.g., localized coarse crackles, rhonchi, clubbing) and help differentiate from other chronic sputum-producing conditions (e.g., asthma with mucus hypersecretion or chronic bronchitis). Since no exam data exists yet, and this is a core domain in the Evidence Framework, I must now request targeted physical exam findings — specifically auscultatory and digital signs most associated with bronchiectasis.

[TEST] Please perform and report:  
- Auscultation of posterior lung fields (upper, middle, lower zones bilaterally): presence, location, and character of crackles, rhonchi, or wheezes;  
- Inspection of fingers for digital clubbing;  
- Assessment for cyanosis or signs of chronic hypoxia.

