[THOUGHT] Medications and allergies are now clarified (none reported). HRCT remains the single most critical missing diagnostic piece — without it, bronchiectasis cannot be confirmed or ruled out definitively. Since two prior attempts to retrieve the HRCT report yielded “Not specified”, and the patient confirms no recall of prior imaging, the test has likely never been performed. Per protocol, I must now request HRCT *as a new diagnostic study*, not as a retrieval. This is distinct from prior requests: earlier turns assumed it existed; now I am explicitly ordering it as the next essential test. It is widely available and directly addresses the core diagnostic question.

[TEST] High-resolution chest CT (HRCT) scan of the lungs — please perform and report:  
- Presence and pattern of bronchiectasis (cylindrical, varicose, cystic);  
- Anatomic distribution (lobes/segments involved);  
- Airway wall thickening, mucus plugging, tree-in-bud opacities;  
- Any associated parenchymal abnormalities (e.g., fibrosis, emphysema, nodules).

